PTX tensormap-update-in-smem
"Grouped GEMM: the producer warp edits its shared-memory copy of the tensor map (tensormap.replace on shared::cta, written here as a generic store), copies it to global memory with tensormap.cp_fenceproxy ... release.gpu, then fence.proxy.tensormap::generic.acquire.gpu and a TMA load with the map (CUTLASS sm90_mma_array_tma_gmma_ss_warpspecialized.hpp:716-755, sm90_gemm_array_tma_warpspecialized_cooperative.hpp:636-673, copy_sm90_desc.hpp:350, 431, 464). The load must use the new map. Expected: forbidden."
{
tms=0 @cta 0;
tm=0;
g=5;
d=0 @cta 0;
b=mbarrier(1) @cta 0;
P0:r2=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0                                                                            ;
 st.weak.shared::cta tms, 1                                                                          ;
 tensormap.cp_fenceproxy.global.shared::cta.tensormap::generic.release.gpu.sync.aligned tm, tms, 128 ;
 fence.proxy.tensormap::generic.acquire.gpu tm, 128                                                  ;
 cp.async.bulk.tensor.1d.shared::cluster.global.tile.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes d, g, b, tm, r2    ;
exists
(P0:r2 == 0)
